If you iterate and work together with AI, you can guide it towards good architecture, but that takes time and effort.

I had to tell mine to not use

If (x) then {  
..   
}  
if (!x) then {  
....  
}  

But use if-then-else instead.

I don't have access to fable, but I am wondering if you have to give it a whole specification for it to generate a software one-shot (like in the old waterfall model) which is usable and maintainable.
